# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# MOASYS-Vault — Shows ignore list (EXAMPLE / REFERENCE FILE)
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# Copy this file to `ignored/shows.yaml` (drop the `.example` suffix) and
# uncomment / edit entries below as needed. The real `shows.yaml` is
# gitignored so personal library decisions don't leak into the repo.
#
# Each entry is a path prefix. Any shows-pass warning whose `path` field
# starts with one of these (followed by `/` or end-of-string,
# case-insensitive, separator-normalized) gets silently dropped from
# `output/shows/warnings.json` (and counted in the run summary).
#
# Get paths from `output/shows/warnings.json` and `output/shows/validation-warnings.json`.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ── Silence whole shows you can't fix ───────────────────────────────────────
# When a show has known missing episodes (never released on the format,
# culled by the rights holder, etc.) and you don't want to see the
# `warn_episode_gaps` / `warn_tmdb_episode_count` noise every run.
# - HD/Channel 4 Catchup (2024)
# - HD/Some Reality Show (2020)

# ── Silence one season ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Keeps the rest of the show's warnings live, but drops everything under
# this specific season folder.
# - HD/Some Show (2020)/Season 2
# - UHD/Star Trek Enterprise (2001)/Season 4

# ── Silence a single episode ────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Pin-point: just one file path. Useful when one episode has a legitimate
# quality outlier you've decided to accept.
# - HD/Some Show (2020)/Season 1/Some Show (2020) - S01E05.mp4

# ── Silence by category ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Drop ALL warnings under a category folder.
# - Other HD
# - Other SD
